module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatNeighbourhoodCech
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SheafTensorUnitSmul
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.AwayKFlat
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CompletionCurrying
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CompletionUnitIso

/-!
# The flat-neighbourhood Čech comparison in the derived category

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `φ : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` be a flat homomorphism of sheaves of
commutative rings which is an isomorphism modulo a sheaf of ideals generated by the global
sections `f_1, …, f_r`, and let `Č(f)` be the extended alternating Čech complex of those
sections. [Stacks, Tag 099H] — in this library
`Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.quasiIso_extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeMap` — says
that degreewise extension of scalars `Č(f) ⟶ Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'` is a quasi-isomorphism.

This file reads that statement inside `D(𝒪)`: the degreewise tensor product computes the
derived tensor product `Č(f) ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪'`, because `𝒪'` is a flat sheaf of `𝒪`-modules and hence
K-flat in degree zero, so Tag 099H says that

`Č(f) ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪[0] ⟶ Č(f) ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪'[0]`

is an isomorphism of `D(𝒪)`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.structureSheafToRestrictedRingModule`: the map `𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` of
  sheaves of `𝒪`-modules underlying `φ`, namely `x ↦ x ⊗ 1` followed by `𝒪 ⊗_𝒪 𝒪' ≅ 𝒪'`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorSingleRestrictedRingModuleIso`: derived tensoring
  with `𝒪'[0]` is the degreewise tensor product.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFlat_restrictedRingModule` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isKFlat_restrictedRingModule`: `𝒪'`, read as a sheaf of
  `𝒪`-modules, is flat, hence K-flat in degree zero.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_Q_map_tensorUnitComplexMap_extendedAlternatingCech`:
  [Stacks, Tag 099H] as invertibility in `D(𝒪)` of the degreewise comparison.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_of_isIso_completionFunctor_map`: a map between
  derived-complete objects which becomes invertible after completion is invertible.

## Implementation notes

Tag 099H is stated for a sheaf of commutative rings `O` on a site, and the derived-completion
development is stated for a `RingedSite`; the two are reconciled by
`Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.ringedSite`, exactly as in `CompletionIdempotent.lean`,
whose `tensorAwayExtendedAlternatingCechIso` crosses the same bridge.

Flatness of `φ` is carried as the two instances `PreservesFiniteLimits` and
`PreservesFiniteColimits` of `𝒪 ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'`, which is the form Tag 099H asks for and which
`Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood.isFlatMap_of_preservesFiniteLimitsColimits` turns into the
named flatness predicate.

The degreewise tensor product of a complex with a module in the second variable is
`CochainComplex.KFlatBifunctor.rowComplex`, which is by construction the complex obtained by
applying `· ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'` in each degree; so no bridge is needed between it and
`(sheafTensorRight 𝒪 𝒪').mapHomologicalComplex`, which is the shape Tag 099H produces.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06YQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06YQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06YU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06YU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

open Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood (RestrictedRingModule tensorUnitMap tensorUnitComplexMap)

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u}) [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {O' : Sheaf X.J CommRingCat.{u}} (φ : X.O ⟶ O')

/-- **The map `𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` of sheaves of `𝒪`-modules underlying `φ`.** It is `x ↦ x ⊗ 1`
(`Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood.tensorUnitMap` at the rank-one module) followed by the
identification `𝒪 ⊗_𝒪 𝒪' ≅ 𝒪'` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso`. -/
def structureSheafToRestrictedRingModule :
    SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O) ⟶
      RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ :=
  (tensorUnitMap.{u, u, u} φ
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))).val ≫
    (SheafOfModules.sheafTensorRightUnitIso X.O (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ)).hom

variable
  [PreservesFiniteLimits
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O).flip.obj (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ))]
  [PreservesFiniteColimits
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O).flip.obj (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ))]

omit [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] in
/-- **`𝒪'` is a flat sheaf of `𝒪`-modules.** Flatness of a homomorphism of sheaves of rings is
by definition flatness of its target read over its source, and
`Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood.isFlatMap_of_preservesFiniteLimitsColimits` produces it from
the two exactness instances in which Tag 099H carries flatness. -/
theorem isFlat_restrictedRingModule :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat.{u, u, u, u} (O := X.O)
      (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ) :=
  Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood.isFlatMap_of_preservesFiniteLimitsColimits φ

omit [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}] in
/-- **`𝒪'` placed in degree zero is a K-flat complex of `𝒪`-modules.** The base case of
[Stacks, Tag 06YQ] applied to `isFlat_restrictedRingModule`. -/
theorem isKFlat_restrictedRingModule :
    CochainComplex.KFlatBifunctor.KFlat
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} X.O)
      ((HomologicalComplex.single
        (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj
        (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ)) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.KFlatResolution.kFlat_single_of_isFlat X.O
    (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ)
    (isFlat_restrictedRingModule X φ) 0

section DerivedTensor

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **Derived tensoring with `𝒪'[0]` is the degreewise tensor product.** For every cochain
complex `K` of `𝒪`-modules, `K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪'[0] ≅ (p ↦ K^p ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')` in `D(𝒪)`. This is the
one-sided K-flat comparison of [Stacks, Tag 06YU], whose hypothesis is
`isKFlat_restrictedRingModule`, followed by the collapse of the total complex of a second
factor concentrated in one degree. It is `derivedTensorSingleAwayModuleIso` read at `𝒪'` in
place of `𝒪_f`. -/
def derivedTensorSingleRestrictedRingModuleIso
    (K : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ℤ) :
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor X).obj (DerivedCategory.Q.obj K)).obj
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj
          ((CochainComplex.singleFunctor
            (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) 0).obj
            (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ))) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        (CochainComplex.KFlatBifunctor.rowComplex
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} X.O) K
          (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ)) :=
  (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct X).comparisonRight K _
      (isKFlat_restrictedRingModule X φ) ≪≫
    DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso (CochainComplex.KFlatBifunctor.totalSingleIso
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} X.O) K
      (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ))

variable {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

omit [PreservesFiniteColimits
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O).flip.obj (RestrictedRingModule.{u, u, u} φ))] in
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099H] as an isomorphism of `D(𝒪)`.** Under the hypotheses of that tag —
`φ` flat, an isomorphism `𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'` compatible with the projections, and `ℐ` locally
generated by the global sections `f_1, …, f_r` — degreewise extension of scalars
`Č(f) ⟶ Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'` becomes invertible in `D(𝒪)`.

The hypothesis is the conclusion of Tag 099H. That tag states it for the composite
`Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeMap`, whose second factor
identifies the target with the Čech complex of the images of the `f_k`; that factor is an
isomorphism of complexes, so the first factor alone is a quasi-isomorphism. -/
theorem isIso_Q_map_tensorUnitComplexMap_extendedAlternatingCech
    (hq : QuasiIso
      (Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeMap X.O f φ)) :
    IsIso (DerivedCategory.Q.map
      (tensorUnitComplexMap.{u, u, u} φ (extendedAlternatingCech X f))) := by
  rw [← DerivedCategory.isIso_Q_map_iff_quasiIso,
    show Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeMap X.O f φ =
      tensorUnitComplexMap.{u, u, u} φ (extendedAlternatingCech X f) ≫
        (Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeIso
          X.O f φ).hom from rfl,
    DerivedCategory.Q.map_comp] at hq
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_right _
    (DerivedCategory.Q.map
      (Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.extendedAlternatingCechBaseChangeIso X.O f φ).hom)

/-- **A map of derived-complete objects which becomes invertible after completion is already
invertible.** The completion map `K ⟶ K^∧` is natural and is invertible at a derived-complete
object (`isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections`), so the
naturality square at `g` writes `g` as a composite of three invertible maps.

This is how a computation carried out after completion — where the Čech formula for the
completion functor makes [Stacks, Tag 099H] available — returns a statement about the objects
themselves. -/
theorem isIso_of_isIso_completionFunctor_map
    {A B : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))}
    (g : A ⟶ B)
    (hA : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) A)
    (hB : IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) B)
    (hg : IsIso ((completionFunctor X f).map g)) : IsIso g := by
  have hA' := isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections X f A hA
  have hB' := isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections X f B hB
  have h1 : IsIso (g ≫ (completionUnit X f).app B) := by
    rw [show g ≫ (completionUnit X f).app B =
      (completionUnit X f).app A ≫ (completionFunctor X f).map g from
        (completionUnit X f).naturality g]
    infer_instance
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_right g ((completionUnit X f).app B)

end DerivedTensor

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
